> 1. What is riding good for?

Gives you bonuses when you're wielding a lance, might make you faster,
gives you greater carrying capacity, might allow you to fly (if riding a
dragon, for example).

> 2. Why is some armor not automatically identified when put on, and
> some is?! Quite random...

Magical armour is only identified if the effects are obvious (speed boots,
for example). Some mundane armour has the same description when identified
and when unidentified, so identifying is unnecessary.

> 3. Why are some food rations in your inventory rotten and some isn't?
> Again, quite random. Do food rations rot in your inventory or are some
> rotten before one picks the up?

I think, but I may be wrong, that cursed rations are always rotten. Good
rations don't rot, I think. It may be (but I don't have the source ready)
that every ration eaten has a random chance of being rotten.

> 4. In the status area, my strenght was indicated 18/02. What does this
> mean?

It means it's higher than 18, but lower than 19. Your strenght will go up
to 18/99, then to 18/**, next to 19, 20, ... Note that strength of 19 or
higher can normally be reached by magical means only, and not every race
can get a strength higher than 18 (which is the same as 18/00). Elves, for
example, can get to 18/50, but no higher, IIRC.

> 5. What is the difference between wearing and eating rings?

Try it in real life. :-)

Wearing a ring confers the effect of the ring.

Eating a ring *may*, with 1/3 chance, confer the effect of the ring,
permanently. Some rings never confer the effect when eaten, or confer a
different effect, for game balance reasons.

For example, a ring of free action will confer free action when worn, but
will confer sleep resistance when eaten.

> 6. How does one use identify scrolls properly? Some can identify more
> than one item when read, but it is impossible to set the
> order/priority of the object I want to identify, because It alway
> identifies the selected iventory items from to top to bottom. So, if I
> am more curious of what this ring is, but in order not towaste the
