> multi-identify-scroll, I shouls select further objects in the
> inventory, before clicking OK. But if these object are above the ring,
> the will be identified first! I hate that... :-(

All object that you haven't identified yet appear in a list (at least in
the tty interface I am using), preceded by a letter. Just press the letter
you want to identify.

If you are eligable to identify more than one item, you will get a second
chance, and so forth.

If you're using another interface, this will probably work differently,
but you should be able to pick items from the list presented.

> 7. Why am I sometimes asked "Really attack the XYZ-Monster?"? And
> sometimes I am not promted, eventhough it's the same type of monster.
> Quite random...

Use the / command followed by the arrow keys and the . key to look at
monsters. You'll notice that some are created peacefully. They won't
attack you, can you'll be asked for confirmation to attack them. Attacking
peaceful monsters is bad for your alignment, which may eventually result
in your god no longer liking you.

It's not random at all.

> 8. Sometime I see "peaceful watchmen". Suddenly if I break open a door
> nearby, he becomes hostile (and these guys, especially the watch
> captains are very deadly), even if there is nothing in the room!?

They just don't like you destroying their town. They also mind if you cut
down trees or empty fountains.

> 9. What is this story about "luck" (eg. you were unlucky/very
> unlucky/luck/etc.)?

Luck is an internal variable, which you'll see only when you quaff a
potion of enlightenment, or by other magical means, or at end of game.

If ranges from -10 to +10, usually, and influences lots of random events
in the game, for example your searching ability. A character with -10 luck
has *huge* difficultiy finding secret doors, while a character with +10
might detect them just while walking by, for example.

When you're not carrying a luckstone, your luck will always gyrate back to
zero in time (so negative *and* positive luck will eventually disappear if
you don't take measures).

